@@ -381,3 +381,35 @@
 Because it is launched through the system dynamic loader, `main.zig` calls
 `prctl(PR_SET_NAME, "reach")` to fix `/proc/self/comm` (and make `pidof reach`
 work).
+
+## Optional agent control
+
+Reach creates no command socket by default. Set `REACH_AGENT_SOCKET` to an
+absolute path in a private runtime directory to enable agent protocol 1. The
+existing `reach.sock` panel stream stays read-only and unchanged.
+
+The agent endpoint uses Unix `SOCK_SEQPACKET`. Each packet is one UTF-8 command
+(no newline required); each response is a JSON object with `ok` and, on failure,
+`error`. Only peers with the same Unix UID are accepted. Requests are limited to
+256 bytes and eight concurrent peers. This is a same-user control interface,
+not an application or filesystem sandbox. Anyone running as that user already
+has access to their apps; keep the parent directory mode 0700. There is no
+shell-execution command. Malformed commands never run as shell text.
+
+Commands:
+
+- `list`: protocol version, Reach PID, and every managed window, including
+  windows on hidden desktops. IDs are monotonic within this Reach process;
+  discard them when the process/session changes. Geometry is output-local.
+- `focus ID`: select the window's output/desktop and focus it.
+- `desktop N`: change the selected output's desktop (1–9).
+- `geometry ID X Y WIDTH HEIGHT`: set a mapped non-fullscreen window floating
+  and assign its geometry. Client minimum sizes can affect the rendered size.
+- `close ID`: request that the client close the named window.
+
+Mutations are queued and revalidated during a river manage sequence. `ok` means
+the WM applied the request; it does not guarantee the application finished
+rendering, accepted a size, saved a file, or agreed to close. Inspect subsequent
+state/screenshots for those assertions. Unknown or closed IDs return an error.
+No commands modify the normal desktop unless that desktop explicitly enables
+this endpoint and a client explicitly connects to it.
